{"role":"assistant","content":"Diagnosis confirmed. Two stacked bugs, exactly matching the evidence:\n\n1. **The job fails every run**: `nightly-review.err` shows `Not logged in · Please run /login` before every crash — the plist sets only `PATH`, no `USER`, so `claude` can't find its keychain login under launchd.\n2. **The failure reporter dies before speaking**: line 19 `status=$?` — in zsh `status` is read-only, so the script aborts on the spot, before the `FAILED` notification at line 22. `runs = 6` with 12 error lines (6 runs × 2 errors) and `last exit code = 1` confirm it.\n\nNow the fixes. First the zsh script:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_jfyyXVTFDsYrJXNZVHBZlfQl","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/private/tmp/h-vvLLuJ/bin/nightly-review.zsh\",\"old_string\":\"claude -p \\\"$PROMPT\\\" --output-format text > \\\"$OUT\\\"\\nstatus=$?\\n\\nif [ $status -ne 0 ]; then\\n  \\\"$NOTIFY\\\" \\\"nightly review FAILED (exit $status), see $OUT\\\"\\n  exit $status\\nfi\\n\\n\\\"$NOTIFY\\\" \\\"nightly review done: $(head -c 300 \\\"$OUT\\\")\\\"\",\"new_string\":\"print -r -- \\\"$PROMPT\\\" | claude -p --output-format text > \\\"$OUT\\\"\\nrc=$?\\n\\nif [ $rc -ne 0 ]; then\\n  \\\"$NOTIFY\\\" \\\"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc), see $OUT\\\"\\n  exit $rc\\nfi\\n\\n\\\"$NOTIFY\\\" \\\"nightly review done: $(head -c 300 \\\"$OUT\\\")\\\"\\necho \\\"nightly review finished in ${SECONDS}s\\\"\"}"}}]}
